[agent] f5 correlates 0.993 with the label — an order of magnitude higher than every other feature. The class-conditional ranges confirm it: for label=0, f5 ∈ [−0.428, 0.398] (mean ≈ 0.0); for label=1, f5 ∈ [2.064, 2.833] (mean ≈ 2.5). The two distributions don't overlap at all, giving essentially perfect separation — the signature of a feature derived from post-outcome data.
[agent] **Answer: f5.**
